From: Abhishek Kunati <itsmekunati@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:21:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] octet: new network magic, address prefixes and bech32
 HRPs; drop Bitcoin seeds

Magic: main e38fb16d, testnet d5a2913c, testnet4 c7b4e91a, regtest f1d68b4e.
Base58: main P2PKH/P2SH/WIF 115/117/247 (o.../p...), all test networks 68/70/207.
Bech32 HRP: oct (main), toct (testnet/testnet4/signet), octrt (regtest).
BIP32 extended-key version bytes are intentionally unchanged (see
docs/consensus-changes.md). Removes Bitcoin DNS seeds, fixed seeds,
nMinimumChainWork and defaultAssumeValid. Signet magic is still derived from the
default (Bitcoin) challenge; main/testnet/testnet4/signet genesis blocks are
still Bitcoin's and are not usable Octet networks yet.
